id: searx-hermetic-e2e
title: Make the E2E suite self-contained by default
description: "Start the existing mock SearXNG server automatically when E2E_SEARXNG_URL is not supplied so test:e2e does not depend on a developer daemon."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: developer-experience,e2e,reliability,testing
created_at: "2026-07-16T17:16:53.271Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-21T22:32:09.375Z"
deadline: "2026-07-18T17:16:53.271Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-16T17:18:02.208Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "bun run test:e2e passes on a host without SearXNG listening on port 8080; an explicit E2E_SEARXNG_URL still overrides the mock; teardown releases all temporary server and filesystem resources"
definition_of_ready: The failing clean-host command and existing mock server helper are confirmed.
parent: searx-repository-audit
reviewer: repository-owner
risk: medium
confidence: 98
sprint: 2026-07-recovery
release: next
reporter: codex-root
severity: medium
environment: "Clean developer or CI host without SearXNG at localhost:8080"
repro_steps: "Ensure port 8080 has no SearXNG service and run bun run test:e2e."
resolution: "Automatic mock lifecycle removes the implicit localhost:8080 dependency."
expected_result: The E2E suite provisions its own deterministic backend unless an explicit endpoint is provided.
actual_result: "The suite configures localhost:8080 and multiple search/format tests fail with fetch failed."
affected_version: 2026.3.6-3
fixed_version: next
component: tests/e2e
regression: false
customer_impact: Contributors cannot reliably run the documented E2E quality gate on clean machines.
